# inv-patch: 20-l1-trfree
# purpose: L1 oracle, tracker-free Mode D completion: with SPDK_INV_TRFREE=1 Mode-D IO qpairs allocate cids from a compact LIFO stack and carry the nvme_request pointer in descriptor w4 (echoed by the device in record w0), so submit and completion skip the tracker, the free_tr and outstanding_tr lists and the tr[cid] lookup. It also introduces the inv lever architecture every later lever follows: one hot byte inv_flags in the existing 2-byte hole after nvme_pcie_qpair.flags (INV_F_* bits set once at IO qpair construct, 0 = every lever off; a static assert locks offsetof(qpair) = 112 in the lean layout), all other lever state at the struct tail, env caches primed by a load-time constructor, and the stock hot paths diverting on inv_flags (one load + branch per poll and per submit) to noinline lever functions (inv_process_completions, marked hot and reached through a cold one-jmp trampoline so GCC keeps the stock block layout of the poll function; inv_trfree_submit, a tail call) while the stock completion loops and the shared poll tail stay unchanged
# safety: UNSAFE
# breaks: abort, timeout and teardown of in-flight Mode-D IO; iterate_requests, the timeout check and the abort walk do not see trfree IO; nvme_pcie_qpair_reset does not re-seed the stack (in-flight IO across a reset is lost); one cb_fn per req (no split IO); an IO qpair with the env set fails ineligible requests with -ENOTSUP (over 128 KiB or non-RW; logged once per process) instead of using a tracker, whose cid would collide with the stack; incompatible with Mode E (not enabled there); per-IO cycle records are not taken on this path. §4 L evidence: one stderr line per Mode-D IO qpair at construct, "INV_TRFREE qid=N cids=K", and at destroy "INV_TRFREE qid=N all K cids returned at destroy", or an ERROR line counting lost and extra cids (a push onto a full stack is counted, never written)
# env: SPDK_INV_TRFREE=1 (default off)
# base: 00-spin.diff,01-floor.diff,10-walk.diff,11-deadstores.diff,12-residue.diff,13-iport.diff
