+/*
+ * inv lever architecture (I4 oracles; 20-l1-trfree introduces it, every later lever follows it).
+ * Goal: with every lever env unset, the inv-levers hot paths equal inv-stock.
+ * - One hot byte, inv_flags, sits in the 2-byte hole after `flags`, so no stock field moves
+ *   (offsetof(qpair) is locked by the static assert after the struct).
+ * - Its INV_F_* bits are set once, at IO qpair construct, from the env; 0 = every lever off.
+ * - All other lever state lives at the struct tail.
+ * - Stock hot paths test inv_flags once (one load + branch per poll, per submit) and divert to
+ *   noinline lever functions (the poll path through a cold trampoline, so GCC keeps the stock
+ *   block layout); the stock loops and the shared poll tail stay unchanged.
+ * - A lever whose bit reaches inv_process_completions() must handle its completions there.
+ */
+#define INV_F_TRFREE	0x01u	/* 20-l1-trfree: Mode D, cid stack, req rides in w4 */
+/* 0x02u..0x80u: later levers */
+
 /* PCIe transport extensions for spdk_nvme_qpair */
